WEBVTT

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:19.120
Who told you to put that shachihoko on the roof?!

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:22.080
You want that to represent us?!

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:25.170
Now, now, Mamoru. Don't be so uptight!

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:28.380
Everyone already knows you do great work.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.800
How cute! Like daddy, like daughter!

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:31.800
Right, Hime?

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:34.420
Well, if you're going to gang up on me...

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:36.430
That's no shachihoko, though...

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:38.550
Shachiho<i>kid</i>, if anything.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:41.310
Shachiho<i>kid</i>? You're shachiho<i>killin'</i> me!

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:46.270
Don't worry. It'll be as good as new.

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:48.770
It's all right. I've had enough.

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:52.440
Racing's gotten... painful.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:56.700
It happens.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.790
You like shachihoko that much?

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:04.040
Yeah, I love them.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:07.420
I'm going to make the golden shachi for the castle one day.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:09.540
It's everyone's guardian god, you know?

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:14.550
You love them, huh?

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:27.190
It's so pretty!

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:30.770
Tomoki, you can have this!

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:34.650
It's thanks for saving me, okay?

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:40.530
Then you can have this.

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:44.160
Huh? They're the same.

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:48.420
It's thanks for helping me
remember something important.

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:49.500
Hm?

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:52.540
This stone is called the "Star of the Circuit".

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:53.800
What's yours called, Himeko?

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.340
Hm? Um...

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:00.300
I know, I'll call it Shachihokid Stone!

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:07.560
I feel like I'm going crazy

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:13.360
I like nice songs

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:17.780
and I want you to listen to them too

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:22.450
Whenever

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:28.410
I sing a song

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:32.000
I hear a voice coming from the microphone

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.420
wishing me the best

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:37.170
I want you

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:38.720
to hear it too

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:39.550
Good luck!

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:43.720
You can't show your love

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:49.230
just with niceties

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:54.110
That won't provide comfort

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:58.490
Whenever I say something

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:04.570
out of the ordinary

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:07.910
in my heart

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:10.370
I wish you the best

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:12.920
I want you

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:14.540
to hear that line

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:15.540
Good luck!

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:34.810
Lightning Speed

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:35.900
You're the captain, Tomoki?
Lightning Speed

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:36.400
You're the captain, Tomoki?

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:37.730
Then—

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:40.240
We weren't the ones who broke the shachihoko.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:43.700
I can see why we ended up taking the fall for it though.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:45.620
Also... Sorry!

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:50.790
I impersonated you to ask a peacebroker for help.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:52.960
I couldn't let my squad know,

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:55.080
but they found out anyway...

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:58.090
Apparently, they want this stone as payment.

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:02.470
I thought I'd use some of the luck from that guardian god you talked about.

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:05.930
I'm sorry. I know this was a gift from you and all...

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:06.850
I see.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:11.730
Hey girls! I bagged us another customer!
You should've told me when you gave me a ride in the bike taxi.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:12.140
Oh, yeah.
Hey girls! I bagged us another customer!

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:12.850
Oh, yeah.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.480
I couldn't believe you'd gotten so pretty.

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:21.650
Huh?

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:24.610
No, I mean—uh... Your dad asked me to do it!

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:26.110
R-Right...

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:27.320
Wait long?

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:29.700
Oh baby! I can feel the love tonight!

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:32.410
My, my, my! Make sure to invite me to the wedding, 'kay?

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:34.160
Ma'am, please! Not now!

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:36.710
I-It must be hard being the captain...

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:39.250
They give it to whoever's fastest.

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:40.800
I'm just a figurehead.

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:44.930
The fastest? Then you were able to become the Star of the Circuit?

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:46.010
Huh?

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:48.430
Oh, yeah.

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:53.100
And why hasn't that star been shooting across any races recently?

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:57.270
Your boys were always too swept up in your races to cause any trouble back then.

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:58.270
Huh?

00:04:58.270 --> 00:05:01.530
Anyway, are you ready to start making those guardian gods?

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:03.360
You went on a journey to train, didn't you?

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:06.570
Oh... yeah.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:09.870
There she is!

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:10.530
Chi!

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:12.660
So cold...

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:15.000
Where were you?

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.960
When I woke up...

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:24.210
Wait, Chi? Why are you so cold?

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:26.420
I'll start the bath.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:30.100
Yukina, can you bring something hot...

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:33.060
Huh? Yukina?

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:36.810
Where could Chiaya be?

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:39.860
Maybe we should slow down, Nozo—

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:41.980
Should what?

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:44.690
Huh? Wh-Who are you people?

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:46.490
Who're <i>you?</i>

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:52.330
'Kay, Ai. Take care of Chi.

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:54.240
Now Yukippe?

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:57.000
She'll be back eventually.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.710
Huh? Who'd be calling this late?

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:04.300
Um, this is Mach... ountain...

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:05.380
Huh?!

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:11.090
Damn them Mie punks.

00:06:11.090 --> 00:06:13.180
This is the last straw!

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:13.930
We refuse to
serve old Mie

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:13.970
We refuse to
serve old Mie

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:14.010
We refuse to
serve old Mie

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:14.060
We refuse to
serve old Mie

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:14.100
We refuse to
serve old Mie

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:14.140
Cafe
We refuse to
serve old Mie

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:17.560
Citizens of old Aichi may not ride here

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:18.310
The circuit is
for Mie's motorcycles.

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:25.820
W-We've got to tell Mr. Dandy!

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:29.200
Oh, Himeko. And...

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:33.160
Are you Maccha Green's subs?

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:37.700
Where am I?

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:40.460
There aren't any landmarks or anything.

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:47.800
Oh, this is...

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:53.300
I apologize. I can't believe they used motorcycles as tools to fight...

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:55.600
We did the same thing.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:59.480
They won't stop unless I race them.

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:04.150
Letting their anger and hatred control you won't make anything better.

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:08.900
I still can't believe that child has grown into the fine young man before me today.

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:10.990
I've watched your races.

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:13.320
Thank you very much.

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:15.160
You haven't been racing recently, have you?

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:19.080
People aren't quite as excited about the annual Tenmusu GP without their young star.

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:22.830
Racing started to feel empty.

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:26.290
There was no one who could compete with me.

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:29.260
What a shame.

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:33.390
U-Um... If the two of you know each other,

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:38.810
then won't you, as captains, discuss how to make the people of this nation get along?

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:40.930
Then, when it works out, you can give us the stone—

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:41.520
Ai!
Then, when it works out, you can give us the stone—

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:43.900
But isn't that how it works?

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:47.820
This stone is the payment, right?

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:50.690
Um, yes, apparently...

00:07:50.690 --> 00:07:53.700
All right. Take it and do what you can to help them.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:54.740
Score!

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:55.870
Himeko!

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:58.990
Well, I <i>am</i> apparently the client.

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:03.040
Besides, I don't need it anymore.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:04.250
Hime?

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:07.000
Uncle, Auntie, what's wrong?

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:09.460
They admitted Mamoru last night.

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:13.340
Said he strained his back.
Can you take these up to him?

00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:17.010
Sorry, but can you?

00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:20.390
Himeko.

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:24.520
As a shachihoko artisan—as one of the people making our guardian gods,

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:27.270
there's something you can do to help.

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:30.280
Isn't that why you came home?

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:34.700
But... I was getting ahead of myself.

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:44.120
Chief, Dandy.

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:46.920
You sure you wanna cancel the Tenmusu GP?

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:48.420
We have no choice.

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:52.090
It would be dangerous to hold the race when the citizens are this emotional.

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:55.470
Then let's have a race to settle the score instead.

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:58.970
A one-on-one match between Vigilante Squad
Captains with the right to rule on the line!

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:00.510
I told you, we're not going to—

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:01.680
Um...

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:06.100
How about we all sit down and think of a new name for the country first?

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:06.810
Huh?!
Huh?!

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:10.940
If we could decide on a name, don't you think we'd get along a little better?

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:13.320
Everyone would have the same attachment to it, too.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:15.400
Um, for example... um...

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:19.320
"Friendly Republic", or "Smile Federation"...

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:23.040
Or "Land of Shachihoko and Circuits"...

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:25.540
Quit talkin' nonsense!

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:26.960
Butt out, outsider!

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:31.290
All right. I'll accept your request.

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:32.210
Mr. Dandy?!

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:34.300
It's all on you now, Captain.

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:35.880
I'll be at HQ!

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:41.220
Oh, Yukippe!

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:44.930
Chiaya! I'm so glad...

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:47.640
See? Told ya she'd be back!

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:51.480
Indeed. Because I'm not bad with directions or anything.

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:56.990
The captain will never give his okay, Vice Cap'.

00:09:57.240 --> 00:09:59.490
Don't worry, I've got a plan!

00:10:01.490 --> 00:10:02.660
Him?

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:04.200
Motoya Daijiro.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:08.580
The legendary rider who retired long before you debuted.

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:10.750
That's who Dandy really is.

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:14.130
Didn't you always say it was your dream to race him?

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:16.970
But I heard he disappeared.

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:18.170
Take a closer look.

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:19.680
Look like anyone?

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:22.930
Well, I can't see his face,

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:24.850
but now that you mention it...

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:27.100
Now challenge the legend!

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:27.930
Okay!

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:31.520
Hahaha!

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:33.820
Gotcha, you moron!

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:36.730
Dandy's just an old dude at a diner!

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:38.490
What? You lied to me?!

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:39.700
No duh!

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:42.030
All I needed was that stamp!

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:43.280
Tie him up!

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:49.750
Mach-ountain

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:51.670
The captain, Suzuka Tomoki is withdrawing?
Mach-ountain

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:52.330
The captain, Suzuka Tomoki is withdrawing?

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:55.000
Then for the upcoming race, you, the vice captain will—

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:55.920
Darn right.

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:55.960
Aichi
Mie

00:10:56.300 --> 00:11:00.300
The dawn of my victory is when
I'll declare Mie to be the ones in charge!

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:04.600
Mr. Dandy, what do you have to say in response?

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:07.560
Old Aichi. Old Mie.

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:10.020
I would like to find a better solution for our coexistence.

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:10.810
Hey, we got the stone already.
Let's move on to the next place!
I would like to find a better solution for our coexistence.

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:13.100
That is why I race.
Hey, we got the stone already.
Let's move on to the next place!

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:14.060
Hey, we got the stone already.
Let's move on to the next place!

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:15.900
Besides, Mr. Dandy said not to get involved any—

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:17.940
We can't do that, Ai.

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:20.950
We have to help bring peace somehow first.

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:23.450
How are we supposed to help in this situation?

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:24.990
I don't know, but...

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:26.830
For Table 3.

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:31.460
It's wrong to take something we didn't earn.

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:35.630
Oh no, I spilled it!
She's too honest.

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:38.200
Now that I think about it,
can Mr. Dandy even ride a motorcycle?

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:40.220
I don't think I've ever seen him riding one.

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:40.950
<b>Nagoya
Castle
Suzuka Circuit
Matsusaka City</b>

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:43.510
It will be a one-on-one road race.
<b>Nagoya
Castle
Suzuka Circuit
Matsusaka City</b>

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:47.420
From Matsusaka, they'll go to Kisosaki—
the reclaimed land at the old border.
<b>Nagoya
Castle
Suzuka Circuit
Matsusaka City</b>

00:11:47.420 --> 00:11:50.710
That's where they'll pick up what they want to put on Nagoya Castle.
<b>Nagoya
Castle
Suzuka Circuit
Matsusaka City</b>

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:52.850
Then it's a mad dash to the castle to win.
<b>Nagoya
Castle
Suzuka Circuit
Matsusaka City</b>

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:57.150
So does that mean it doesn't have to be shachihoko?

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:57.900
What?!

00:11:57.900 --> 00:12:01.360
The castle tower has to have shachihoko!

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:04.490
But the Uotora artisan strained his back, didn't he?

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:06.820
Then, who else could make them?

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:13.410
Oh! I found this backpack.

00:12:13.410 --> 00:12:15.170
Does that say fish?

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:16.880
I think this is...

00:12:18.750 --> 00:12:20.380
We have to bring it to him.

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:22.630
Golden Shachi General Hospital

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:28.180
Himeko?

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:31.430
I'm sorry I slapped you.

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:36.480
I can't believe I made you say that.

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:41.690
You've loved shachihoko since you were little, haven't you?

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:46.610
You spent your childhood in the workshop, copying what I did...

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:48.490
Hey, Himeko.

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:52.660
The soul of the artisan is in the shachihoko.

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:55.870
That's why they're all different.

00:12:56.120 --> 00:13:01.130
<i>You're</i> the only one that can make your shachihoko.

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:04.840
Everyone's waiting for it.

00:13:04.840 --> 00:13:06.550
So make one.

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:08.510
Make it with everything you've got!

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:12.770
Huh? You're—

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:15.930
Sir!

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:24.530
Dear...

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:25.360
Those girls...

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:27.530
They're working in Hime's place?

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:44.260
We did it!

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:47.880
An orca?!

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:50.260
Did we get it wrong?

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:52.560
Orca and shachihoko are different things.

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:54.430
Isn't it just a sea animal?!

00:13:56.350 --> 00:13:59.270
Please leave this to me!

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:06.070
I don't really know what I would
want to put on the top of the castle.

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:10.200
Shachihoko really make the most sense on top of a castle, don't you think?

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:11.160
Yeah.

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:14.660
You morons! It doesn't have to be a Mie specialty!

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:14.790
Everyone, will you look at this?

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:17.540
It's just gotta piss off those Aichi twats!
Everyone, will you look at this?

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:18.210
Everyone, will you look at this?

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:21.920
This looks like the shachihoko that will be used in the race against old Mie.

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:22.290
Exclusive live coverage from the Uotora home!!
<b>Breaking News</b>

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:24.800
They must be exhausted.
Exclusive live coverage from the Uotora home!!
<b>Breaking News</b>

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:27.970
Everyone is sleeping.
Exclusive live coverage from the Uotora home!!
<b>Breaking News</b>

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:35.310
They just finished!

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:35.930
This is the completed Uotora shachihoko!

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:37.430
Uotora's New Masterpiece?!
<b>Breaking News
This is the completed Uotora shachihoko!</b>

00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:39.190
What?!

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:40.480
Wha...

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:45.020
Uotora's New Masterpiece?!
Breaking News
I wonder if the Aichi Tenmusus plan to put this on the Nagoya Castle tower?

00:14:45.020 --> 00:14:46.880
No, stop! Don't show it!
Breaking News
